 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A software design principle in which a module keeps its internal details private behind a stable interface, so changes inside it do not affect the rest of the program.",
 "description": {
  "text": "Information hiding is the software design principle of separating the design decisions most likely to change, so that a stable interface shields the rest of the program if those decisions change.",
